524
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:40,000
In order to honor these Olympians who had,

525
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:46,000
who had labored till exhaustion to be able to be the best at what they are.

526
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:50,000
Paul said, I have labored over you.

527
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:58,000
So, please don't grumble, don't argue, but trust the Lord and see what he's going to do.

528
00:28:58,000 --> 00:29:00,000
It's a powerful word.

529
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:06,000
Now, I know some of you are thinking, give me a break, Matt.

530
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:10,000
I mean, my question is, are you more like Alan or more like Paul?

531
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:14,000
Matt, if you give me that one, I'm probably more like Alan than I am like Paul.

532
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:16,000
I get it.

533
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:18,000
You know, give me a break, so I'm not like Paul.

534
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:20,000
Okay, that's fair.

535
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:23,000
So, Paul says, well, and it's not just me.

536
00:29:23,000 --> 00:29:27,000
But if you'll follow with me to verse 19.

537
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:34,000
I hope in the Lord Jesus to send Timothy to you soon.

538
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:40,000
That I may also be cheered when I receive news about you.

539
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:48,000
I have no one else like him who will show genuine concern for your welfare.

540
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:54,000
For everyone looks out for their own interests, not that of Jesus Christ.

541
00:29:56,000 --> 00:30:01,000
So, are you more, okay, I'm not more like Paul than Alan.

542
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:04,000
Are you more like Alan or Timothy?

543
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:09,000
Timothy was the go-to guy for Paul.

544
00:30:09,000 --> 00:30:14,000
He's who Paul sent to Thessalonica, 1 Thessalonians 3:8.

545
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:17,000
He's the one who Paul sent to Corinth.

546
00:30:17,000 --> 00:30:18,000
You remember Corinth?

547
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:19,000
They were the really messed up church.

548
00:30:19,000 --> 00:30:23,000
Paul sent him to Corinth, 1 Corinthians 4:17.

549
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:25,000
Paul sends him to Philippi.

550
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Why?

551
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:29,000
Because there's no one else like him.

552
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:36,000
His concern is for Jesus above his own concerns.

553
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:46,000
When I was first starting church planting 35 years ago, we went and listened to Bob Logan, who was kind of the guru of church planting at the time.

554
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:57,000
And I remember a lot of the things he taught, but one of the things he said, he said, you know, unfortunately, most Christians, their favorite radio station is WIIFM.

555
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:00,000
What's in it for me?

556
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:01,000
What's in it for me?

557
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:13,000
We all have this tendency, and I would be remiss if I didn't admit that I too have this tendency to look out for my own concerns.

558
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:27,000
But Paul, at the end of his life, is saying, I've run the race, and I may be poured out, but I rejoice, and I'm glad.

559
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:38,000
And I've sent Timothy, who rejoices, and is glad, because his concern is one thing: Jesus.

560
00:31:39,000 --> 00:31:41,000
I think it's an important question to ask ourselves.

561
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:43,000
Are we more like Alan?

562
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:46,000
Or like Timothy?

563
00:31:46,000 --> 00:31:54,000
Hebrews 13:23 tells us that Timothy actually ended up a prisoner for Christ's sake as well.

564
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:55,000
But I know what you're thinking.

565
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:56,000
Come on, Matt.

566
00:31:56,000 --> 00:31:57,000
Give me a break.

567
00:31:57,000 --> 00:31:59,000
I'm not called to be a pastor like Timothy.

568
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:01,000
I'm not Paul.

569
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:02,000
I'm not a pastor.

570
00:32:02,000 --> 00:32:03,000
Give me a break.

571
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:04,000
Okay, Paul says, that's fine.

572
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Let's go to the third person.

573
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:08,000
Verse 25.

574
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:12,000
He said, so I'd like to come.

575
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:13,000
Don't know if I can.

576
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:14,000
I'd like to send Timothy.

577
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:15,000
Don't know if I can.

578
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:20,000
But I think it's necessary to send back to you Epaphroditus.

579
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:22,000
And he's not a pastor.

580
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:23,000
He's not an apostle.

581
00:32:23,000 --> 00:32:26,000
Now, he's just a brother, co-worker, and fellow soldier.

582
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:30,000
It's a fascinating story of him.

583
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:34,000
Paul started the Philippian church.

584
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:36,000
And by the way, Timothy was there when he started the church.

585
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:40,000
And they are probably the closest church to him.

586
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:51,000
It's the only church that Paul allowed to receive an offering and give it to his missionary band to be able to do the work that they were doing.

587
00:32:51,000 --> 00:32:55,000
This Philippians is considered the gospel of joy.

588
00:32:56,000 --> 00:33:06,000
There's almost this smile in Paul's heart as he's sitting in prison about to die, writing to this church that he cares about so much, that he loves so much.

589
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:08,000
They have this reciprocity.

590
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:17,000
And Epaphroditus was there because the Philippian church, for the third time now, has taken up this offering, and they've sent it to Paul.

591
00:33:17,000 --> 00:33:19,000
But back then, you can't Venmo it.

592
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:23,000
And so you send someone with it.

593
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:40,000
And Epaphroditus was the one who was given the offering to travel through a scary world to finally get to where Paul is in Rome while he's in prison and to hand him the gift.

594
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Listen to what Paul says about him.

595
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:57,000
But I think it's necessary to send back to you Epaphroditus, my brother, co-worker, fellow soldier, who is also the messenger whom you sent to take care of my needs.

596
00:33:58,000 --> 00:34:05,000
For he longs for all of you, is distressed because he hurt, you heard he was ill, indeed he was ill, and almost died.

597
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:12,000
But God had mercy on him, and not on him only, but also on me, to spare me sorrow upon sorrow.

598
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:20,000
Therefore, I am more eager to send him to you, so that you will see him again, and may be glad, and I may have less anxiety.

599
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:30,220
So welcome him in the Lord with great joy and honor, people like him, because he almost died for the work of Christ.

600
00:34:30,220 --> 00:34:45,620
In a little bit, I'm going to call Tara up to lead us in prayer for our brothers in India, particularly the Kumars who we support, and I'll say a little more about that.

601
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:51,360
There in Andhra Pradesh, and I mean, if this is India, Andhra Pradesh is over here.

602
00:34:51,360 --> 00:34:55,620
Well, the state right above it, it was Orissa, it's now Odessa.

603
00:34:55,620 --> 00:35:08,140
A friend of mine, Bajoy Raul, was a pastor that went into the jungles of Orissa and began to share the gospel.

604
00:35:08,140 --> 00:35:13,240
His testimony is, when he first went to the jungles, this was, again, 40, 50 years ago,

605
00:35:13,880 --> 00:35:16,860
he went in and people were naked and living in trees.

606
00:35:16,860 --> 00:35:19,880
But he knew that Jesus died for them.

607
00:35:19,880 --> 00:35:22,720
He knew it was going to be hard, but he began to share the gospel.

608
00:35:22,720 --> 00:35:29,260
And they began to respond to the gospel, and he realized this was bigger than him.

609
00:35:29,260 --> 00:35:34,020
And so, while he cared for them, he also went back to his home area,

610
00:35:34,020 --> 00:35:39,740
and he began to disciple and, not evangelize, these guys were already believers,

611
00:35:39,740 --> 00:35:46,120
but discipled them to be evangelists and witnesses, because there was so much need in Orissa,

612
00:35:46,120 --> 00:35:47,880
he could never get to it.

613
00:35:47,880 --> 00:35:50,540
And he had the smart idea of multiplying.

614
00:35:50,540 --> 00:35:53,920
You teach others who can teach others who can teach others.

615
00:35:53,920 --> 00:35:58,120
And so he taught these folks, and they would go into Odessa,

616
00:35:58,120 --> 00:36:00,960
and they would share the gospel, and it was exploding.

617
00:36:02,320 --> 00:36:05,020
When Bejoy came to the States to raise some funds,

618
00:36:05,020 --> 00:36:08,280
he was telling the stories of what God was doing,

619
00:36:08,280 --> 00:36:12,380
the miracles of how God had protected him and protected his evangelists,

620
00:36:12,380 --> 00:36:15,280
but also how hard it was and how difficult it was.

621
00:36:15,280 --> 00:36:17,260
But it was for the gospel of Jesus Christ.

622
00:36:17,260 --> 00:36:19,660
And as he was sharing in the congregation,

623
00:36:19,660 --> 00:36:22,880
the executive director of our mission board was there with him,

624
00:36:22,920 --> 00:36:24,640
and they were talking and sharing.

625
00:36:24,640 --> 00:36:31,500
And he was talking about these evangelists who knew that about 70% of them

626
00:36:31,500 --> 00:36:36,600
were going to end up with malaria if they went into Orissa.

627
00:36:36,600 --> 00:36:38,560
It was mosquito-ridden.

628
00:36:38,560 --> 00:36:43,040
They would use nets and that kind of stuff, but it was hard.

629
00:36:43,040 --> 00:36:46,720
And he talked about them being willing to go,

630
00:36:46,820 --> 00:36:52,180
and he said, about 15 minutes into his message as he's sharing this story,

631
00:36:52,180 --> 00:36:54,620
one guy raised his hand, and he said,

632
00:36:54,620 --> 00:36:57,520
Brother Bejoy, I don't get it.

633
00:36:57,520 --> 00:37:01,760
If they knew they were going to get malaria, why would they go?

634
00:37:01,760 --> 00:37:08,140
Bejoy was dumbfounded.

635
00:37:08,140 --> 00:37:10,220
He didn't want to offend these folks,

636
00:37:10,220 --> 00:37:14,820
but he just finally, he looked at Jack, the mission director,

637
00:37:15,240 --> 00:37:17,000
like, I don't know how to answer that.

638
00:37:17,000 --> 00:37:19,240
And Jack said,

639
00:37:19,240 --> 00:37:24,520
because they have no other way to hear the gospel of Jesus Christ.

640
00:37:24,520 --> 00:37:32,480
The story of Paul ends with the realization

641
00:37:32,480 --> 00:37:34,600
that he was all in.

642
00:37:34,600 --> 00:37:38,520
And not only was he all in,

643
00:37:38,520 --> 00:37:40,280
but the people he discipled, Timothy's,

644
00:37:40,280 --> 00:37:42,560
they were all in.

645
00:37:44,120 --> 00:37:46,660
And not only the Timothys who became pastors,

646
00:37:46,660 --> 00:37:53,020
but the people from the churches where he planted churches were all in.

647
00:37:53,020 --> 00:37:58,620
And their concern was primarily for the gospel of Jesus Christ.

648
00:37:58,620 --> 00:38:02,780
For the grace of God that they had received,

649
00:38:02,780 --> 00:38:05,340
the response was not, should I go?

650
00:38:05,340 --> 00:38:07,760
The response was, how can I not go?

651
00:38:09,300 --> 00:38:12,360
Keith Green, 40 years ago, at a concert,

652
00:38:12,360 --> 00:38:15,400
he said, you know, the command has already been given to go.

653
00:38:15,400 --> 00:38:17,820
The question shouldn't be, should I go?

654
00:38:17,820 --> 00:38:20,600
The question should be, why should I stay?

655
00:38:23,600 --> 00:38:25,860
Now, I'm not trying to call you all into missions.

656
00:38:25,860 --> 00:38:29,020
Ryan would be really bummed at me if you all left tomorrow.

657
00:38:29,020 --> 00:38:31,620
Well, no, he'd probably be excited.

658
00:38:31,620 --> 00:38:34,620
He'd probably be excited.

659
00:38:35,460 --> 00:38:37,580
Because I think Ryan would lay down his ministry

660
00:38:37,580 --> 00:38:39,720
to see the gospel spread across the globe.

661
00:38:39,720 --> 00:38:44,180
So, are we more like Alan?

662
00:38:44,180 --> 00:38:49,800
Are we more like Paul or Timothy or Epaphroditus?

663
00:38:51,260 --> 00:38:52,360
It's a fair question.

664
00:38:52,360 --> 00:38:54,600
It's a question that,

665
00:38:54,600 --> 00:38:59,600
well, back to my illustration from the very beginning.

666
00:38:59,600 --> 00:39:04,740
The missionary executive director that stood up

667
00:39:04,740 --> 00:39:09,080
and had 90 seconds to present a ministry

668
00:39:09,080 --> 00:39:12,420
to over a billion people who don't know Jesus

669
00:39:12,420 --> 00:39:15,720
with an attempt to not just raise funds,

670
00:39:15,720 --> 00:39:16,600
but recruit people.

671
00:39:16,600 --> 00:39:18,360
It's like a good friend of mine.

672
00:39:19,440 --> 00:39:20,780
He was working in Spain,

673
00:39:20,780 --> 00:39:22,120
which is in the 1040 window.

674
00:39:22,120 --> 00:39:25,740
And a pastor told him,

675
00:39:25,740 --> 00:39:28,620
I want you to talk about what you're doing,

676
00:39:28,620 --> 00:39:30,520
but I don't want you asking for any money, Bruce.

677
00:39:30,520 --> 00:39:32,400
Bruce was like, okay.

678
00:39:32,400 --> 00:39:34,640
So, when he was giving his talk,

679
00:39:34,640 --> 00:39:35,200
he got up there.

680
00:39:35,200 --> 00:39:36,560
And this, I mean, I heard him do it.

681
00:39:36,560 --> 00:39:39,060
He said, I just want you to know

682
00:39:39,060 --> 00:39:40,240
that I'm not here for your money.

683
00:39:40,240 --> 00:39:41,860
I don't want your money.

684
00:39:41,860 --> 00:39:44,140
I mean, you know, you do what God tells you,

685
00:39:44,140 --> 00:39:45,000
but I'm not here for your money.

686
00:39:45,000 --> 00:39:46,960
I need your children.

687
00:39:49,440 --> 00:39:54,040
That's the all-in gospel.

688
00:39:54,040 --> 00:39:59,040
Tara, can you come?

689
00:39:59,040 --> 00:40:00,700
We're going to pray for the Kumars.

690
00:40:00,700 --> 00:40:04,200
I think you know that part of the philosophy

691
00:40:04,200 --> 00:40:06,180
of outreach and ministry here

692
00:40:06,180 --> 00:40:10,400
is that we choose just a few ministries,

693
00:40:10,400 --> 00:40:12,000
and we focus there.

694
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:12,720
So the kids' club,

695
00:40:12,720 --> 00:40:14,320
we do tons of stuff at the kids' club,

696
00:40:14,400 --> 00:40:15,880
and constantly looking for ways

697
00:40:15,880 --> 00:40:18,080
to be Jesus to the kids' club.

698
00:40:18,080 --> 00:40:20,000
By the way, if you're convicted,

699
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:21,660
but you say, I can't go to India,

700
00:40:21,660 --> 00:40:23,620
great, can you read to some kids

701
00:40:23,620 --> 00:40:24,440
over at the kids' club?

702
00:40:24,440 --> 00:40:26,100
Start there.

703
00:40:26,100 --> 00:40:31,200
We work with a ministry in,

704
00:40:31,200 --> 00:40:32,940
I think it's in Tennessee, is that right?

705
00:40:32,940 --> 00:40:36,400
Where they basically rescue women

706
00:40:36,400 --> 00:40:39,040
out of trafficking, sex trafficking,

707
00:40:39,460 --> 00:40:41,260
and try to give them identity back

708
00:40:41,260 --> 00:40:41,920
and life back.

709
00:40:41,920 --> 00:40:43,400
But the third,

710
00:40:43,400 --> 00:40:44,760
and that's kind of our Jerusalem

711
00:40:44,760 --> 00:40:45,560
and our Judea,

712
00:40:45,560 --> 00:40:47,040
but our third is to the uttermost

713
00:40:47,040 --> 00:40:47,740
parts of the world,

714
00:40:47,740 --> 00:40:49,240
and so we've chosen to focus

715
00:40:49,240 --> 00:40:49,920
on the Kumars

716
00:40:49,920 --> 00:40:52,200
because, first of all,

717
00:40:52,200 --> 00:40:54,240
the Kumars are part of our tribe,

718
00:40:54,240 --> 00:40:56,940
part of our family of churches,

719
00:40:56,940 --> 00:40:58,980
but they also have a similar

720
00:40:58,980 --> 00:41:00,340
philosophy of ministry.

721
00:41:01,300 --> 00:41:03,160
They say, we want to find

722
00:41:03,160 --> 00:41:04,660
a real need for people

723
00:41:04,660 --> 00:41:06,040
who are hurting,

724
00:41:06,040 --> 00:41:08,160
and we want to provide

725
00:41:08,160 --> 00:41:10,080
for that need in a way

726
00:41:10,080 --> 00:41:11,900
that displays the love of Jesus

727
00:41:11,900 --> 00:41:14,140
so that then they're intrigued

728
00:41:14,140 --> 00:41:15,960
to ask, why are you doing this?

729
00:41:15,960 --> 00:41:16,500
And I can say,

730
00:41:16,500 --> 00:41:17,300
because of what Jesus

731
00:41:17,300 --> 00:41:18,180
has done for me.

732
00:41:18,180 --> 00:41:20,240
How can I not do it?

733
00:41:20,240 --> 00:41:22,940
And so they teach women to sew.

734
00:41:22,940 --> 00:41:23,800
Most of these women

735
00:41:23,800 --> 00:41:24,640
have been abandoned

736
00:41:24,640 --> 00:41:25,300
